G2532.def:
καί, 
conj., 
and 
__I. Copulative. 
__1. Connecting single words; 
__(a) in general: Matthieu 2:18, 16:1, Marc 2:15, Luc 8:15, Hébreux 1:1, al. mult.; repeated before each of the terms in a series, Matthieu 23:23, Luc 14:21, Romains 7:12, 9:4, al.
__(b) connecting numerals (WM, §37, 4): Jean 2:20, Actes 13:20; 
__(with) joining terms which are not mutually exclusive, as the part with the whole: Matthieu 8:33, 26:59, Marc 16:17, Actes 5:29, al. 
__2. Connecting clauses and sentences: Matthieu 3:12, Actes 5:21, al. mult.; esp. 
__(a) where, after the simplicity of the popular language, sentences are paratactically joined (WM, §60, 3; M, Pr., 12; Deiss., LAE, 128ff.): Matthieu 1:21, 7:25, Marc 9:5, Jean 10:3, al.; 
__(b) joining affirmative to negative sentences: Luc 3:14, Jean 4:11, IIIJhn.10; 
__(with) consecutive, and so: Matthieu 5:1, 23:32, Hébreux 3:19, al.; after imperatives, Matthieu 4:19, Luc 7:7, al.; 
__(d) = καίτοι, and yet: Matthieu 3:14, 6:26, Marc 12:12, Luc 18:7 (Field, Notes, 72), 1 Corinthiens 5:2, al.; 
__(e) beginning an apodosis (= Heb. וְ; so sometimes δέ in cl.), then: Luc 2:21, 7:12, Actes 1:10; beginning a question (WM, §53, 3a): Marc 10:26, Luc 10:29, Jean 9:36.
__3. Epexegetic, and, and indeed, namely (WM, §53, 3c): Luc 3:18, Jean 1:16, Actes 23:6, Romains 1:5, 1 Corinthiens 3:5, al.
__4. In transition: Matthieu 4:23, Marc 5:1, 21, Jean 1:19, al.; so, Hebraistically, καὶ ἐγένετο (וַי:הִי; also ἐγένετο δέ), Marc 1:9 (cf. Luc 5:1; V. Burton, §§357-60; M, Pr., 14, 16). 
__5. καὶ . . . καί, both . . . and (for τε . . . καί, see: τε); 
__(a) connecting single words: Matthieu 10:28, Marc 4:41, Romains 11:33, al.; 
__(b) clauses and sentences: Marc 9:13, Jean 7:28, 1 Corinthiens 1:22, al. 
__II. Adjunctive, also, even, still: Matthieu 5:39, 40; Marc 2:28, al. mult.; esp. with pron., adv., etc., Matthieu 20:4, Jean 7:47, al; ὡς κ., Actes 11:17; καθὼς κ., Romains 15:7; οὑτω κ., Romains 6:11; διὸ κ., Luc 1:35; ὁ κ. (Deiss., BS, 313ff.), Actes 13:9; pleonastically, μετὰ κ.. (Bl., §77, 7; Deiss., BS, 265f,), Philippiens 4:3; τί κ., 1 Co 15:29; ἀλλὰ κ., Luc 14:22, Jean 5:18, al.; καίγε (M, Pr., 230; Burton, §437), Actes 17:27; καίπερ, Hébreux 5:8; κ. ἐάν, see: ἐάν.
ἐάν, contr. fr. εἰ ἄν, 
conditional particle, 
representing something as "under certain circumstances actual or liable to happen," but not so definitely expected as in the case of εἰ with ind. (Bl., §65, 4; cf. Jean 13:17, 1 Corinthiens 7:36), if haply, if; 
__1. with subjc. (cl.); 
__(a) pres.: Matthieu 6:22, Luc 10:6, Jean 7:17, Romains 2:25, 26 al.; 
{ __(b) aor. (= Lat. fut. pf.): Matthieu 4:9 16:26 (cf. ptcp. in Luc 9:25; M, Pr., 230), Marc 3:24, Luc 14:34, Jean 5:43, Romains 7:2, al.; = cl. εἰ, with opt., Jean 9:22 11:57, Actes 9:2; as Heb. אִם = ὅταν, Jean 12:32 14:3, I Jean 2:28 3:2, Hébreux 3:7" (LXX) . 
__2. C. indic, (as in late writers, fr. Arist. on; see WH, App., 171; VD, MGr. 2, App., §77; Deiss., BS, 201f., LAE, 155, 254; M, Pr., 168, 187; Bl., §65, 4); 
__(a) fut.: Matthieu 18:19 T, Luc 19:40, Actes 7:7; 
__(b) pres.: 1 Thessaloniciens 3:8 (see Milligan, in l.). 
__3. With other particles: ἐ. καί (Bl., §65, 6), Galates 6:1; ἐ. μή (M, Pr., 185, 187; Bl., l.with), with subjc. pres., Matthieu 10:13, 1 Corinthiens 8:8, Jacques 2:17, 1 Jean 3:21; aor., Matthieu 6:15, Marc 3:27, Jean 3:3, Romains 10:15, Galates 1:8 2:16 (see Lft., Ellic., in ll.); ἐ. τε . . . ἐ. τε, [in LXX for אִם . . . אִם, Esther 19:13, al.,] Romains 14:8. 
__4. = cl. ἄν (which see) after relat. pronouns and adverbs (Tdf., Pr., 96; WH, App., 173; M, Pr., 42f.; Bl., §26, 4; Mayser, 152f.; Deiss., BS, 202ff.): ὃς ἐ., Matthieu 5:19, Marc 6:22, 23 Luc 17:32, 1 Corinthiens 6:18, al.; ὅπου ἐ., Matthieu 8:19; ὁσάκις ἐ., Apocalypse 11:6; οὗ ἐ., 1 Corinthiens 16:6; καθὸ ἐ., 2 Corinthiens 8:12; ὅστις ἐ., Galates 5:10.

G2560.def:
κακῶς
(κακός), 
adv., [in LXX: Wis.18:19, 4Ma.6:17.al.; κ. εἰπεῖν, ἐρεῖν (אָרַר, קָלַל pi.), Exode 22:28 (27), Lévitique 19:14, Ésaïe 8:21; κ. ἔχειν (חָלָה, Eze.34:4, al. ;] 
badly, ill; 
__(a) in physical sense: κ. ἔχειν, to be ill, Matthieu 4:24 8:16 9:12 14:35 17:15, Marc 1:32, 34 2:17 6:55 5:31 7:2; πάσχειν, Matthieu 17:15 (WH, mg.); δαιμονίζεσθαι, Matthieu 15:22; κακοὺς κ. ἀπολέσει (as frequently in cl., see LS, see word; MM, Exp., xv), evil that they are, he will evilly, etc., Matthieu 21:41; 
__(b) in moral sense, wrongly (1Ma.7:42, 4Mac, l.with, al.): κ. λαλεῖν, Jean 18:23; είπεῖν, with accusative of person(s), Actes 23:5; αἰτεῖσθαι, Jacques 4:8,†

G2563.def:
κάλαμος, -ου, ὁ 
[in LXX chiefly for קָנֶה, Ésaïe 42:3, Eze.40:3 ff., al. ;] 
a reed: Matthieu 11:7 12:20" (LXX) Luc 7:24; hence, accusative, to its various uses, 
__(a) a reed-pipe, flute; 
__(b) a reed-staff, staff (cf. 4Ki.18:21, ῥάβδος καλαμίνη): Matthieu 27:29-30, 48, Marc 15:19, 36; 
__(with) a measuring reed or rod (Ez, l.with): Apocalypse 11:1 21:15-16; 
__(d) a writing reed, a pen: III Jn 13 (cf. Milligan, NTD, 9, 7).†

G2596.def:
κατά (bef. a vowel κατ᾽, καθ᾽; on the frequently neglect of elision, see Tdf., Pr., 95; WH, App., 146a), 
prep. with genitive, accusative, 
down, downwards. 
__I. C. genitive (WM, §47, k; Bl., §42, 2). 
__1. C. genitive of thing(s), in local sense; 
__(a) down, down from: Matthieu 8:32, Marc 5:13, Luc 8:33, 1 Corinthiens 11:4; 
__(b) throughout (late usage; Bl, l.with): κ. ὅλης κ.τ.λ., Luc 4:14 23:5, Actes 9:31 10:37; 
__(with) in a peculiar adjectival phrase: ἡ κ. βάθους, deep or extreme poverty, 2 Corinthiens 8:2. 
__ __2. C. genitive of person(s), usually in hostile sense; 
__(a) against (in cl. only after verbs of speaking, witnessing, etc.): opposite to ὑπέρ, Marc 9:40; μετά, Matthieu 12:30; after ἐπιθυμεῖν, Galates 5:17; λαλεῖν, Actes 6:13; διδάσκειν, Actes 21:28; ψεύδεσθαι, Jacques 3:14; after verbs of accusing, etc., Matthieu 5:23, Luc 23:14, Romains 8:33, al.; verbs of fighting, prevailing, etc., Matthieu 10:35, Actes 14:2, 1 Corinthiens 4:6, al.; 
__(b) of swearing, by: όμνυμι κ. (BL, §34, 1), He 6:13,16, cf. Matthieu 26:63. 
__II. C. accusative (WM, §49d; BL, §42, 2). 
__1. Of motion or direction; 
__(a) through, throughout: Luc 8:39 9:6 10:4, Actes 8:1, 36 al.; 
__(b) to, towards, over against: Luc 10:32 (Field, Notes, 62), Actes 2:1o 16:7, Galates 2:11, Philippiens 3:14, al.; 
__ __(with) in adverbial phrases, at, in, by, of: κατ᾽ οἶκον, at home, Actes 2:46; κατ᾽ ἰδίαν (see: ἴδιος); καθ᾽ ἑαυτόν, Actes 28:16, Romains 14:22, Jacques 2:17; with pron. of person(s), Actes 17:28 18:15, Romains 1:15, Éphésiens 1:15, al. 
__2. Of time, at, during, about: Actes 8:26 12:1 19:23, Romains 9:9 Hébreux 1:10, al. 
__3. Distributive; 
__(a) of place: κ. τόποὐς, Matthieu 24:7, al.; κ. πόλιν, Luc 8:1, 4 al.; κ. ἐκκλησίαν, Actes 14:23. 
__(b) of time: κ. ἔτος, Luc 2:41; ἑορτήν, Matthieu 27:15, al.; 
__(with) of numbers, etc.: καθ᾽ ἕνα πάντες, 1 Corinthiens 14:31 (on καθ᾽ εἷς, see: εἷς); κ. ἑκατόν, Marc 6:40; κ. μέρος, Hébreux 9:5; κ. ὄνομα, Jean 10:3. 
__4. Of fitness, reference, conformity, etc.; 
__(a) in relation to, concerning: Romains 1:3, 4 7:22 9:3, 5, 1 Corinthiens 12:6 10:18, Philippiens 1:12; κ. πάντα, Actes 17:22, Colossiens 3:20, 22 Hébreux 2:17 4:15; 
__(b) according to, after, like: Marc 7:5, Luc 2:27, 29 Jean 7:24 Romains 8:4 14:15, Éphésiens 2:2, Colossiens 2:8, Jacques 2:8, al. 
__III. In composition, κ. denotes, 
__1. down, down from (καταβαίνω), etc.), hence, metaphorically; 
__(a) victory or rule over (καταδουλόω, -κυριεύω, etc.); 
__(b) "perfective" action (M, Pr., 111ff.). 
__2. under (κατακαλύπτω), etc.). 
__3. in succession (καθεξῆς). 
__4. after, behind (καταλείπω). 
__5. Hostility, against (καταλαλέω).
